<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Project Cooum river model</name><Placemark><name>Cooum River, Kesavaram anicut to the sea</name><description>Estimated: Hand-traced through geocoded towns and bridges, about 62 km here (official length about 65 km). Follows the real course only roughly; trace from OpenStreetMap before engineering use. Source: CRRT (length), Mapbox geocoding (waypoints)</description><LineString><coordinates>79.7618,13.0214,0 79.79,13.03,0 79.8139,13.04,0 79.8418,13.056,0 79.852,13.08,0 79.8602,13.0968,0 79.885,13.1,0 79.91,13.098,0 79.935,13.097,0 79.9614,13.1,0 79.99,13.1,0 80.02,13.098,0 80.05,13.097,0 80.075,13.095,0 80.098,13.091,0 80.118,13.078,0 80.14,13.072,0 80.16,13.07,0 80.185,13.066,0 80.2008,13.0668,0 80.212,13.0715,0 80.225,13.0738,0 80.236,13.074,0 80.2438,13.0719,0 80.252,13.07,0 80.258,13.0695,0 80.263,13.0675,0 80.269,13.0684,0 80.272,13.0705,0 80.275,13.0724,0 80.279,13.0712,0 80.282,13.07,0 80.2845,13.0689,0 80.289,13.0665,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Official restoration stretch: Paruthipattu to the mouth (32 km)</name><description>Sourced: Extent is from CRRT; the line uses the approximate trace. Source: CRRT</description><LineString><coordinates>80.09801,13.091,0 80.118,13.078,0 80.14,13.072,0 80.16,13.07,0 80.185,13.066,0 80.2008,13.0668,0 80.212,13.0715,0 80.225,13.0738,0 80.236,13.074,0 80.2438,13.0719,0 80.252,13.07,0 80.258,13.0695,0 80.263,13.0675,0 80.269,13.0684,0 80.272,13.0705,0 80.275,13.0724,0 80.279,13.0712,0 80.282,13.07,0 80.2845,13.0689,0 80.289,13.0665,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pilot stretch 1: Napier Bridge to river mouth (0.5 km)</name><description>Sourced: End points from the DPR tender news; line drawn on the approximate trace. Source: DT Next, Oct 2026</description><LineString><coordinates>80.28445,13.06892,0 80.2845,13.0689,0 80.289,13.0665,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pilot stretch 2: Periyar Bridge to Swami Sivananda Salai (1.2 km)</name><description>Estimated: Named in the DPR tender; where Sivananda Salai meets the river is estimated (1.2 km below Periyar Bridge). Source: DT Next, Oct 2026</description><LineString><coordinates>80.27496,13.07238,0 80.275,13.0724,0 80.279,13.0712,0 80.282,13.07,0 80.2845,13.0689,0 80.28526,13.0685,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pilot stretch 3: Link Road to Dams Road (2 km)</name><description>Estimated: Named in the DPR tender; Dams Road end placed at the Anna Salai bridge, Link Road end estimated 2 km upstream. Source: DT Next, Oct 2026</description><LineString><coordinates>80.25113,13.0702,0 80.252,13.07,0 80.258,13.0695,0 80.263,13.0675,0 80.269,13.0684,0 80.26906,13.06844,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kesavaram anicut (source of the Cooum)</name><description>Sourced: Mapbox lists this as 'Pudu Kesavaram Dam', Arakkonam. Taken as the anicut where the Cooum leaves the Kosasthalaiyar; confirm on site. Source: Mapbox Search</description><Point><coordinates>79.7618,13.0214,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Napier Bridge</name><description>Sourced: Bridge position from Mapbox. Source: Mapbox Search</description><Point><coordinates>80.28449,13.06889,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Periyar Bridge</name><description>Sourced: Bridge position from Mapbox. Source: Mapbox Search</description><Point><coordinates>80.27503,13.07237,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Anna Salai (Mount Road) bridge, Dams Road</name><description>Sourced: Bridge position from Mapbox. Source: Mapbox Search</description><Point><coordinates>80.26902,13.06838,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>River mouth at Marina (sand bar forms here)</name><description>Estimated: Mouth closes with sand most of the year; dredged repeatedly. Source: IIT Madras Tech Talk</description><Point><coordinates>80.289,13.0665,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Koyambedu treatment plant: 45 MLD tertiary (TTRO) water</name><description>Sourced: Less than 20 MLD of 45 MLD is used today. Releasing spare water as year-round base flow (~580 mcft a year) keeps the river moving and the mouth open. Plant pin from Mapbox. Source: World Bank; Citizen Matters</description><Point><coordinates>80.20076,13.0674,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Proposed treated-water outfall to river</name><description>Proposal (this project): Short release pipe; route not surveyed. Source: Project research 02</description><LineString><coordinates>80.20076,13.0674,0 80.2008,13.0668,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Pudumavilangai check dam (existing)</name><description>Estimated: 2.3 m high, 100 m wide, ₹7.8 cr; irrigates Kadambathur, Satharai, Agaram. Position estimated near the named village. Proposal: add adjustable shutters (₹0.5 to 1.5 cr each, +30 to 50% storage). Source: News / WRD</description><Point><coordinates>79.876,13.0985,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Putlur check dam (existing)</name><description>Estimated: One of five existing dams that held at least 130 mcft after a good monsoon. Position estimated near the named village. Proposal: add adjustable shutters (₹0.5 to 1.5 cr each, +30 to 50% storage). Source: News / WRD</description><Point><coordinates>79.945,13.0975,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Paruthipattu check dam (existing)</name><description>Estimated: Upstream end of the 32 km restoration stretch. Position estimated near the named village. Proposal: add adjustable shutters (₹0.5 to 1.5 cr each, +30 to 50% storage). Source: News / WRD</description><Point><coordinates>80.098,13.091,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Soranjeri check dam (sanctioned 2022, ₹5.62 cr)</name><description>Estimated: Sanctioned by WRD G.O. 12 (2022). Site position not public; placed on the river between Aranvoyal and Paruthipattu. Source: WRD G.O. 12</description><Point><coordinates>80.02,13.098,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>New shuttered check dam (candidate)</name><description>Proposal (this project): Candidate for 2 to 3 more shuttered dams in years 1 to 3, near farm tanks. Source: Project research 02</description><Point><coordinates>79.83,13.048,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>New shuttered check dam (candidate)</name><description>Proposal (this project): Candidate site, as above. Source: Project research 02</description><Point><coordinates>79.99,13.1,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Upper-zone irrigation tank cluster (~80 tanks, ~9,940 ha)</name><description>Estimated: 80 tanks with ~9,940 ha registered farmland in the sub-basin; 61 rural tanks irrigate ~6,630 ha in Kancheepuram, Thiruvallur and Vellore blocks. Outline is a rough zone, not individual tanks. Source: IAMWARM Cooum DPR</description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>79.74,13.0,0 79.8,12.985,0 79.9,13.03,0 80.0,13.06,0 80.06,13.07,0 80.06,13.13,0 79.98,13.145,0 79.88,13.135,0 79.8,13.11,0 79.745,13.07,0 79.74,13.0,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>North training wall (proposed, 265 m)</name><description>Estimated: WRD plan with NIOT design, about ₹70 cr for both walls. Needs CRZ clearance, ~18 months. Alignment drawn schematically. Source: The Hindu via inkl</description><LineString><coordinates>80.2884,13.0678,0 80.2908,13.068,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>South training wall (proposed, 310 m)</name><description>Estimated: As above. Get the angle and height right: earlier Cooum walls failed. Source: The Hindu via inkl</description><LineString><coordinates>80.2884,13.0652,0 80.2912,13.0654,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Boating weir candidate: Chetpet</name><description>Proposal (this project): Inflatable rubber or gated weir, 1 to 1.5 m, ₹10 to 30 cr; lies flat in floods. Build only after clean base flow exists. Source: Project research 02</description><Point><coordinates>80.24372,13.07192,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Boating weir candidate: Aminjikarai</name><description>Proposal (this project): Inflatable rubber or gated weir, 1 to 1.5 m, ₹10 to 30 cr; lies flat in floods. Build only after clean base flow exists. Source: Project research 02</description><Point><coordinates>80.22509,13.0738,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Boating weir candidate: Koyambedu</name><description>Proposal (this project): Inflatable rubber or gated weir, 1 to 1.5 m, ₹10 to 30 cr; lies flat in floods. Build only after clean base flow exists. Source: Project research 02</description><Point><coordinates>80.2009,13.06684,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cleaning-robot dock 1</name><description>Proposal (this project): Charging and trash-offload point for river-cleaning robots and boats; placed beside bridges and weirs for road access. Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.28744,13.06733,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cleaning-robot dock 2</name><description>Proposal (this project): Charging and trash-offload point for river-cleaning robots and boats; placed beside bridges and weirs for road access. Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.27602,13.07209,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cleaning-robot dock 3</name><description>Proposal (this project): Charging and trash-offload point for river-cleaning robots and boats; placed beside bridges and weirs for road access. Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.26996,13.06907,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cleaning-robot dock 4</name><description>Proposal (this project): Charging and trash-offload point for river-cleaning robots and boats; placed beside bridges and weirs for road access. Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.2448,13.07167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cleaning-robot dock 5</name><description>Proposal (this project): Charging and trash-offload point for river-cleaning robots and boats; placed beside bridges and weirs for road access. Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.2262,13.07382,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cleaning-robot dock 6</name><description>Proposal (this project): Charging and trash-offload point for river-cleaning robots and boats; placed beside bridges and weirs for road access. Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.20191,13.06727,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Napier Bridge entrance</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.28318,13.06948,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Periyar Bridge</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.2738,13.07164,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Anna Salai bridge</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.26771,13.06821,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Pudupet small bridge</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.26164,13.06804,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Egmore entrance</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.25068,13.07031,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Chetpet bridge</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.24239,13.07228,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Shenoy Nagar entrance</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.23455,13.07397,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Aminjikarai bridge</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.22372,13.07357,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Arumbakkam entrance</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.21065,13.07093,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Leased shop cluster: Maduravoyal entrance</name><description>Proposal (this project): Free walk, paid shops. Model: 20 entrances × 10 shops + 15 bridges × 6 shops (~290 shops, 200 sq ft, ₹60 to 150 per sq ft a month). Source: Project research 01</description><Point><coordinates>80.18364,13.06622,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bank-top solar strip (north bank)</name><description>Proposal (this project): About 10 MWp across ~10 km of banks, ~14 GWh a year, ~₹55 cr. Panels on banks and walkway canopies, never on the channel. Source: Project research 02</description><LineString><coordinates>80.2009,13.06754,0 80.212,13.0722,0 80.225,13.0745,0 80.236,13.0747,0 80.2438,13.0726,0 80.24552,13.0722,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bank-top solar strip (south bank)</name><description>Proposal (this project): As above. Source: Project research 02</description><LineString><coordinates>80.2009,13.06614,0 80.212,13.0708,0 80.225,13.0731,0 80.236,13.0733,0 80.2438,13.0712,0 80.24552,13.0708,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bank-top solar strip (north bank)</name><description>Proposal (this project): About 10 MWp across ~10 km of banks, ~14 GWh a year, ~₹55 cr. Panels on banks and walkway canopies, never on the channel. Source: Project research 02</description><LineString><coordinates>80.25001,13.07116,0 80.252,13.0707,0 80.258,13.0702,0 80.263,13.0682,0 80.26725,13.06884,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bank-top solar strip (south bank)</name><description>Proposal (this project): As above. Source: Project research 02</description><LineString><coordinates>80.25001,13.06976,0 80.252,13.0693,0 80.258,13.0688,0 80.263,13.0668,0 80.26725,13.06744,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sewage outfall marker 1 (illustrative)</name><description>Estimated: 118 outfalls found in 2014; 41 plugged by Nov 2025. Exact positions are not public, so these markers only show spread along the 32 km stretch, about one per 1.1 km. Source: Project brief</description><Point><coordinates>80.0